---
title: V0.14 text and numeric formatting
---
# Text and numeric formatting

String lengths and slices count Unicode code points. Numeric formatting uses
the fixed locale separators and bounded pattern syntax.

```amx
dimension Length
unit meter: Length
unit centimeter = 0.01 * meter

let codePointLength = len("A🙂B")
let listLength = len([1, 2, 3])
let combiningSequenceLength = len("é")
let trimmed = trim(" AMX ")
let firstTwo = left("A🙂B", 2)
let lastTwo = right("A🙂B", 2)
let defaultLeft = left("AMX")
let emptyRight = right("AMX", 0)

let groupedUS = format(1234.5, "#,##0.00", "en-US")
let groupedGerman = format(1234.5, "#,##0.00", "de-DE")
let groupedFrench = format(1234.5, "#,##0.00", "fr-FR")
let percentage = format(0.125, "0.0%", "en-US")
let currency = format(-1234.5, "$#,##0.00", "en-US")
let displayedDistance = format(1.25 meter, "0.00")
let displayedCentimeters = format(125 centimeter, "#,##0.00")
```
